13
01:07:42,500 --> 01:07:48,500
Bridesmaids is a 2011 American comedy film directed by Paul Feig
from a screenplay by Annie Mumolo and Kristen Wiig.

14
01:12:55,000 --> 01:13:01,000
It stars Wiig as a woman who experiences a series of misfortunes after being asked to
serve as maid of honor for her best friend, played by Maya Rudolph.

15
01:18:07,500 --> 01:18:13,500
The ensemble cast also features Rose Byrne, Wendi McLendon-Covey,
Ellie Kemper, Melissa McCarthy and Chris O'Dowd.

16
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
Actresses Mumolo and Wiig wrote the screenplay after the latter
was cast in Judd Apatow's comedy Knocked Up (2007).

17
01:28:32,500 --> 01:28:38,500
Upon its theatrical release in the United States on May 13, 2011,
Bridesmaids was a critical and commercial success.

18
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,000
It grossed over $306 million worldwide on a $32.5 million budget, and surpassed
Knocked Up to become the top-grossing Apatow Productions film to date.

19
01:38:57,500 --> 01:39:03,500
At the 84th Academy Awards, McCarthy was nominated for Best Supporting
Actress, and Wiig and Mumolo for Best Original Screenplay.

20
01:44:10,000 --> 01:44:16,000
Bridesmaids has served as a touchstone for discussion about women in comedy.

21
01:49:22,500 --> 01:49:28,500
Several publications have ranked it among the best
comedy films of the 21st century.

22
01:54:35,000 --> 01:54:41,000
The film explores themes of jealousy, parent child
relationship, fight, competition, materialism.

23
01:59:47,500 --> 01:59:53,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
